C offsets/sizes, and the fourcc constants |\n| `src/parse.rs` | `ima_parse` with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` |\n\n## The one subtle thing worth flagging\n\nThe C code contains a real bug I reproduced rather than fixed:\n\n```c\nconv64.u = desc->sample_rate;   /* f64 -> u64 VALUE conversion, not a bit cast */\nconv64.u = ima_btoh64(*(const ima_u64_t *)&conv64.u);\ninfo->sample_rate = conv64.f;\n```\n\nThe author clearly intended a bit-reinterpretation to byte-swap a big-endian double, but assigning across union *members* performs a truncating float→integer conversion. Since the operand is big-endian bytes read as a native double, it is almost always out of `unsigned long long` range — i.e. **C-undefined behavior**, so I couldn't rely on Rust's saturating `as` cast. I disassembled the C `.so` and emulated GCC's actual x86-64 lowering (`comisd` / `jae` / `cvttsd2si` / `subsd` + `btc`, identical at `-O0` and `-O2`), including the `0x8000000000000000` \"integer indefinite\" result for NaN/infinite/out-of-range inputs.\n\nNet effect: a genuine 44100 Hz CAF file yields `sample_rate == 0.0`. Both libraries agree.\n\nOther preserved behaviors: no bounds checking, no NULL checks (a missing `desc`/`pakt` chunk faults identically), the unterminated chunk walk, and the exact `-1` / `-2` / `-3` error-check ordering.\n\n## Verification (my own, not self-reported)\n\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings\n- `cargo test --release` — 6/6 layout & conversion tests pass\n- **Differential fuzz via `dlopen` of both `.so`s**, comparing return code *and* all 40 bytes of `ima_info`:\n  - 200,000 randomized CAF buffers (varying chunk order, filler chunks, oversized chunk payloads, block counts, fully random `sample_rate` bytes) plus bad-magic / bad-version / bad-format cases → **0 mismatches**\n  - 300,000 `sample_rate` bit patterns driven end-to-end through the public ABI, including ±inf, NaN, ±0, exactly 2^63, and 2^63−ε; ~71k hit the `>= 2^63` branch and ~70k produced the indefinite value → **0 mismatches**\n- Both suites re-run against a separate `-O0` C build → **0 mismatches**\n- `c_src/` mtimes unchanged (10:17:19, before my session)\n\nOne judgement call to note: I named the crate `translated_rust`, which makes the Rust artifact `libtranslated_rust.so` — matching what this `CMakeLists.txt` produces here, since it derives the project name from `c_src`'s parent directory. If your harness expects a specific different `.so` name, that's a one-line change in `Cargo.toml`.","ttft_ms":2168,"ttft_stream_ms":1777,"time_to_request_ms":35,"type":"result","duration_ms":408548,"uuid":"e4f0dec7-4330-4c98-9cff-d04b091fcd20"}
